        "verseCount": 22,
        "copyright": "PUBLIC DOMAIN except in the United Kingdom, where a Crown Copyright applies to printing the KJV. See http://www.cambridge.org/about-us/who-we-are/queens-printers-patent"
      },
      {
        "id": "ROM.8.8-ROM.8.29",
        "orgId": "ROM.8.8-ROM.8.29",
        "bibleId": "01b29f4b342acc35-01",
        "bookId": "ROM",
        "chapterIds": [
          "ROM.8"
        ],
        "reference": "Romans 8:8-29",
        "content": [
          {
            "name": "para",
            "type": "tag",
            "attrs": {
              "style": "p"
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "for neither is it able; and those who are in the flesh are not able to please God. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.8",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.8"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And you are not in the flesh, but in the Spirit, if indeed the Spirit of God dwells in you; and if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ—this one is not His; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.9",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.9"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and if Christ [is] in you, the body, indeed, [is] dead because of sin, and the Spirit [is] life because of righteousness, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.10",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.10"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and if the Spirit of Him who raised up Jesus out of the dead dwells in you, He who raised up the Christ out of the dead will also quicken your dying bodies, through His Spirit dwelling in you. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.11",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.11"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "So, then, brothers, we are debtors, not to the flesh, to live according to the flesh; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.12",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.12"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for if according to the flesh you live, you are about to die; and if, by the Spirit, the deeds of the body you put to death, you will live; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.13",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.13"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are the sons of God; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.14",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.14"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for you did not receive a spirit of bondage again for fear, but you received [the] Spirit of adoption in which we cry, “Abba! Father!” ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.15",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.15"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "[This] One—the Spirit—testifies with our spirit, that we are children of God; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.16",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.16"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and if children, also heirs, heirs, indeed, of God, and heirs together of Christ—if, indeed, we suffer together, that we may also be glorified together. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.17",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.17"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "For I reckon that the sufferings of the present time [are] not worthy [to be compared] with the glory about to be revealed in us; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.18",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.18"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for the earnest looking out of the creation expects the revelation of the sons of God; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.19",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.19"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for to vanity was the creation made subject—not of its will, but because of Him who subjected [it]—in hope, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.20",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.20"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "that also the creation itself will be set free from the servitude of the corruption to the liberty of the glory of the children of God; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.21",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.21"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for we have known that all the creation groans together, and travails in pain together until now. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.22",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.22"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And not only [so], but also we ourselves, having the first-fruit of the Spirit, we also ourselves groan in ourselves, expecting adoption—the redemption of our body; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.23",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.23"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for in hope we were saved, and hope beheld is not hope; for what anyone beholds, why does he also hope for [it]? ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.24",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.24"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And if what we do not behold we hope for, through continuance we expect [it]. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.25",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.25"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And in like manner also, the Spirit helps our weaknesses; for what we may pray for, as it is necessary, we have not known, but [this] One—the Spirit—makes intercession for us with unutterable groanings, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.26",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.26"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and He who is searching the hearts has known what [is] the mind of the Spirit, because according to God He intercedes for holy ones. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.27",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.27"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And we have known that to those loving God all things work together for good, to those who are called according to purpose; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.28",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.28"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "because whom He foreknew, He also foreordained, conformed to the image of His Son, that He might be firstborn among many brothers; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.29",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.29"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
